dsh-Go-theme — a client theme for DeepSeek Harness
Package: @dsh-external/dsh-client-ui-theme-go
License: MIT (see LICENSE)
=======================================================================

This theme is an independent visual reimplementation inspired by DSH Go.

Design reference:
  DSH Go — https://github.com/ccch1mneyyy/dsh-Go
  Pinned commit: ca3c4202f0110a9a10311034d532eafd9ee2e290
  License: AGPL-3.0 (source) — no source code was copied
  The reference's theme files note portions derived from PiPilot (MIT),
  Copyright (c) 2026 CikeSeven, https://github.com/CikeSeven/pi_pilot

No brand assets, mascots, character artwork, or README imagery from
DSH Go are included. All visual assets in this package are original.

Colour derivation follows Björn Ottosson's OKLab/OKLCH publication (2020),
which the reference also uses; the matrices are public domain.


What "independent reimplementation" means here
----------------------------------------------

* Design values — colour stops, hue and chroma parameters, radii, spacing
  steps, motion timings, material opacity — are treated as facts, not as
  expression. They were recomputed from those facts by tools/derive-tokens.py
  (an OKLCH implementation written for this project) rather than copied out of
  a source file. tools/check-dart-constants.py compares the two sets of numbers
  for transcription errors; it reads the reference at check time and never
  vendors an upstream file into this repository.

* No Dart file from DSH Go was copied, translated or adapted. The TypeScript in
  src/ is written against the DSH client-plugin API and the palette numbers this
  project derived. Where the desktop web renderer needed different behaviour
  (a real page gradient, two tiers of glass, backdrop-filter only on the
  composer seat), the effect was re-tuned or re-designed, not ported.

* Every surface here is built from official --dsw-* design tokens plus a small
  amount of plugin-owned CSS. There is no image, sprite, font file or icon from
  upstream: icon.svg is drawn for this project.


